    {
     "type": "reading",
     "star": true,
     "title": "The Birdwatcher",
     "paragraphs": [
      "Last Friday, my uncle asked, 'Where shall we go tomorrow?'",
      "'Let's go to the lagoon near Benghazi,' I said. 'There are lots of birds there.'",
      "'Oh, Yousef! You always want to watch birds,' my sister Nada laughed. 'It's boring!'",
      "'No, it isn't. It's a great hobby,' said my uncle.",
      "On Saturday morning, we drove to the lagoon. My uncle stayed by the car, and Nada and I walked along the water. There were hundreds of birds! I took out my binoculars because I wanted to see them better.",
      "'What can you see?' Nada asked. I could see lots of ducks and some small birds. Then I saw a tall pink bird. It was standing on one leg in the water. It had long thin legs and a curved bill.",
      "'Quick, Nada! Take a photo!' I said. Suddenly, a dog ran along the beach and the bird flew away. Under its wings, I could see black feathers.",
      "At home, I looked in my bird book. There it was: a flamingo! I felt so excited. It was the first time I had seen one, and Nada had a photo of it!"
     ]
    }
   ],
